export const SLANG=[{"zh":"躺平","pinyin":"tǎng píng","en":"lie flat / quiet quitting","description":"放棄競爭，降低慾望，選擇最低限度生活方式","sentences":[{"en":"I am done chasing promotions. I am officially lying flat.","zh":"我不再追求升職了，我正式躺平了。"},{"en":"After ten years of grinding, she decided to lie flat and just breathe.","zh":"工作了十年後，她決定躺平，好好喘口氣。"},{"en":"The quiet quitting trend is basically the Western version of lying flat.","zh":"安靜辭職的潮流基本上就是西方版本的躺平。"},{"en":"He is not lazy — he is lying flat on purpose as a form of protest.","zh":"他不是懶——他是故意躺平，作為一種抗議方式。"},{"en":"Lying flat does not mean doing nothing. It means doing less than society expects.","zh":"躺平不是什麼都不做，而是比社會預期做得更少。"},{"en":"She reduced her hours, stopped overtime, and embraced lying flat.","zh":"她減少了工作時間，停止加班，擁抱了躺平。"},{"en":"Lie flat culture is a response to the pressure of modern work life.","zh":"躺平文化是對現代工作生活壓力的一種回應。"},{"en":"I told my boss I was done with overwork. Call it lying flat.","zh":"我告訴我的老闆我不再過度工作了，你可以叫它躺平。"},{"en":"Choosing to lie flat is a quiet form of setting boundaries.","zh":"選擇躺平是一種安靜的設立界限的方式。"},{"en":"She is not a failure — she just chose to lie flat and be happy.","zh":"她不是失敗者——她只是選擇了躺平，讓自己快樂。"}]},{"zh":"內捲","pinyin":"nèi juǎn","en":"involution / rat race","description":"過度競爭、資源內耗，努力卻無法帶來實質進步","sentences":[{"en":"The involution at this company is insane — everyone works sixteen hours a day.","zh":"這家公司的內捲太嚴重了——每個人每天工作十六個小時。"},{"en":"She is so tired of the involution in her industry — it never ends.","zh":"她厭倦了行業裡的內捲——永遠沒有盡頭。"},{"en":"When everyone overworks just to stay in place, that is pure involution.","zh":"當所有人都在過度工作只是為了保住現有位置，那就是純粹的內捲。"},{"en":"The rat race here is brutal. You work more but earn the same.","zh":"這裡的競爭很殘酷，你工作更多，但賺的還是一樣多。"},{"en":"He refused to join the involution and went home at six every day.","zh":"他拒絕參與內捲，每天六點回家。"},{"en":"Involution is when effort no longer leads to meaningful progress.","zh":"內捲是指努力不再帶來有意義的進步的時候。"},{"en":"She dropped out of the rat race and started her own business.","zh":"她退出了內捲競爭，開始了自己的事業。"},{"en":"When the whole industry involutes, individuals suffer the most.","zh":"當整個行業內捲時，個人受苦最深。"},{"en":"Competition is healthy. Involution is destructive.","zh":"競爭是健康的，內捲是破壞性的。"},{"en":"I refuse to participate in the involution just to impress my boss.","zh":"我拒絕為了讓老闆留下深刻印象而參與內捲。"}]},{"zh":"打工人","pinyin":"dǎ gōng rén","en":"office worker / the working class","description":"自嘲打工賺錢的普通上班族","sentences":[{"en":"Every morning I wake up and tell myself: I am just an office worker.","zh":"每天早上我醒來告訴自己：我只是個打工人。"},{"en":"The working class works hard and the bosses take the credit.","zh":"打工人努力工作，老闆們卻拿走功勞。"},{"en":"As an office worker, I dream of one day being my own boss.","zh":"作為一個打工人，我夢想有一天能當自己的老闆。"},{"en":"She jokes she is just a humble worker bee in a giant hive.","zh":"她開玩笑說自己只是大蜂巢裡一個卑微的工蜂。"},{"en":"The office worker grind is real — coffee, commute, repeat.","zh":"打工人的日常是真實的——咖啡、通勤、重複。"},{"en":"He calls himself a blue-collar worker with a white-collar salary.","zh":"他稱自己為領白領薪水的藍領工人。"},{"en":"Nine to five, five days a week — that is the life of the working class.","zh":"九點到五點，每週五天——這就是打工人的生活。"},{"en":"I told my friend: you and I are just workers trying to survive.","zh":"我告訴我朋友：你我只是努力求存的打工人。"},{"en":"Even the most passionate worker can burn out.","zh":"即使是最有熱情的打工人也可能倦怠。"},{"en":"She wears her working-class identity with humour and pride.","zh":"她以幽默和驕傲展示她的打工人身份。"}]},{"zh":"擺爛","pinyin":"bǎi làn","en":"let it rot / giving up","description":"自暴自棄，乾脆不努力，任由事情走向最差結果","sentences":[{"en":"After failing for the third time, she decided to just let it rot.","zh":"第三次失敗後，她決定乾脆擺爛了。"},{"en":"He stopped caring about the project and went full let-it-rot mode.","zh":"他不再關心那個項目，直接進入擺爛模式。"},{"en":"When the system is broken, some people just give up and let it rot.","zh":"當系統出了問題，有些人就選擇放棄，擺爛了。"},{"en":"She jokes she is in let-it-rot mode until her next paycheck.","zh":"她開玩笑說她要擺爛到下個發薪日。"},{"en":"Sometimes letting it rot is a form of self-protection.","zh":"有時候擺爛是一種自我保護的方式。"},{"en":"I am not letting it rot — I am strategically conserving energy.","zh":"我不是在擺爛——我是在策略性地保存能量。"},{"en":"When you are burnt out, giving up feels like the only option.","zh":"當你倦怠時，放棄感覺是唯一的選擇。"},{"en":"He went into full giving-up mode and played games all week.","zh":"他進入了完全擺爛模式，整週打遊戲。"},{"en":"There is a difference between rest and letting it rot.","zh":"休息和擺爛之間有區別。"},{"en":"She snapped out of her let-it-rot phase and started fresh.","zh":"她從擺爛狀態中走出來，重新開始了。"}]},{"zh":"佛系","pinyin":"fó xì","en":"zen attitude / going with the flow","description":"以平和心態面對一切，不強求，隨緣","sentences":[{"en":"She has a very zen attitude — nothing bothers her.","zh":"她有一種非常佛系的態度——什麼都不會讓她心煩。"},{"en":"I am trying to be more zen about things I cannot control.","zh":"我試著對我無法控制的事情更佛系一點。"},{"en":"He takes a very go-with-the-flow approach to life.","zh":"他對生活採取非常隨緣的態度。"},{"en":"Her zen attitude at work is contagious — she calms everyone down.","zh":"她在工作中的佛系態度很有感染力——她讓所有人平靜下來。"},{"en":"Instead of stressing, she goes with the flow and things work out.","zh":"她不是壓力很大，而是隨緣，事情就自然好了。"},{"en":"He is so zen he could sleep through a fire alarm.","zh":"他太佛系了，連火警鈴都能睡過去。"},{"en":"Adopting a zen mindset helped her let go of perfectionism.","zh":"採用佛系心態幫助她放棄了完美主義。"},{"en":"She does not chase results — she is pure go-with-the-flow energy.","zh":"她不追求結果——她是純粹的隨緣能量。"},{"en":"There is wisdom in the zen approach: not everything needs your energy.","zh":"佛系方法有其智慧：不是所有事情都需要你的精力。"},{"en":"He applied for the job with zero expectations — total zen mode.","zh":"他以零期望申請了那份工作——完全佛系模式。"}]},{"zh":"破防","pinyin":"pò fáng","en":"hit hard / walls came down","description":"被某件事觸動情緒防線，忍不住哭或有強烈感受","sentences":[{"en":"That short film totally hit hard — I cried in public.","zh":"那部短片太破防了——我在公共場合哭了。"},{"en":"She said she would not cry but that last scene hit her hard.","zh":"她說她不會哭，但最後那一幕讓她破防了。"},{"en":"This song hits differently when you are going through something.","zh":"當你正在經歷某些事情時，這首歌打動你的方式不同了。"},{"en":"That letter from her dad completely brought her walls down.","zh":"她爸爸的那封信讓她完全破防了。"},{"en":"He has a reputation for being tough but that story hit him hard.","zh":"他以堅強著稱，但那個故事讓他破防了。"},{"en":"Unexpectedly, a children's cartoon made my walls come down.","zh":"意想不到地，一部兒童卡通讓我破防了。"},{"en":"When the documentary showed the elderly couple, everyone's walls came down.","zh":"當紀錄片展示那對老年夫婦時，所有人都破防了。"},{"en":"I did not expect to be hit so hard by a commercial.","zh":"我沒想到一個廣告會讓我這麼破防。"},{"en":"Hitting hard and going viral — that is what good content does.","zh":"破防然後瘋傳——這就是好內容的作用。"},{"en":"She hit hard when she talked about her journey on stage.","zh":"她在台上分享她的旅程時，讓大家都破防了。"}]},{"zh":"社恐","pinyin":"shè kǒng","en":"social anxiety / socially awkward","description":"對社交場合感到焦慮或不舒服","sentences":[{"en":"I am genuinely socially anxious — parties drain me completely.","zh":"我真的有社交恐懼——派對讓我完全精疲力竭。"},{"en":"She is not rude — she is just socially anxious and finds it hard to speak.","zh":"她不是無禮——她只是有社交恐懼，很難開口說話。"},{"en":"He practised what to say for ten minutes before making the phone call.","zh":"他在打電話前練習了十分鐘要說什麼。"},{"en":"Social anxiety makes even small talk feel like a performance.","zh":"社交恐懼讓即使是閒聊都感覺像是表演。"},{"en":"She avoids events with strangers — pure social anxiety mode.","zh":"她避開有陌生人的活動——純粹的社恐模式。"},{"en":"Being socially awkward does not mean you do not like people.","zh":"社交笨拙並不意味著你不喜歡人們。"},{"en":"Texting is great for socially anxious people — time to think.","zh":"發訊息對有社交焦慮的人很好——有時間思考。"},{"en":"I cancelled plans again because my social anxiety kicked in.","zh":"我又取消計畫了，因為我的社交焦慮發作了。"},{"en":"Crowds give me social anxiety — I prefer small gatherings.","zh":"人群給我帶來社交焦慮——我更喜歡小型聚會。"},{"en":"She pushed through her social anxiety and made the first move.","zh":"她克服了社交恐懼，邁出了第一步。"}]},{"zh":"摸魚","pinyin":"mō yú","en":"slacking off / goofing off at work","description":"在工作時間做與工作無關的事","sentences":[{"en":"He spent two hours slacking off watching YouTube at his desk.","zh":"他在辦公桌前摸魚看了兩個小時的 YouTube。"},{"en":"Goofing off at work is fine — everyone needs brain breaks.","zh":"在工作中摸魚沒關係——每個人都需要休息大腦。"},{"en":"She was deep in slacking-off mode when her boss walked by.","zh":"她正在深度摸魚，這時她的老闆走了過來。"},{"en":"I am an expert at looking busy while actually doing nothing.","zh":"我是一個看起來很忙實際上什麼都不做的專家。"},{"en":"When the meeting has no point, slacking off is survival.","zh":"當會議毫無意義時，摸魚是一種生存方式。"},{"en":"He answered all emails in ten minutes then spent the rest goofing off.","zh":"他十分鐘內回覆了所有電子郵件，然後剩下的時間都在摸魚。"},{"en":"A bit of slacking off during the day keeps creativity alive.","zh":"工作中摸魚一點可以保持創造力。"},{"en":"She is goofing off on her phone but still meets every deadline.","zh":"她在手機上摸魚，但每個截止日期都還是能完成。"},{"en":"The art of looking busy while slacking off is underestimated.","zh":"看起來很忙但實際上在摸魚的藝術被低估了。"},{"en":"Remote work made slacking off much harder to define.","zh":"遠程工作讓摸魚的定義更加模糊了。"}]},{"zh":"氛圍感","pinyin":"fēn wéi gǎn","en":"vibes / atmosphere","description":"某個空間或場景給人的特殊感覺或情緒","sentences":[{"en":"That café has such good vibes — dim lights and soft music.","zh":"那家咖啡廳的氛圍感很好——昏暗的燈光和柔和的音樂。"},{"en":"She knows how to set the mood — candles, playlist, ambiance.","zh":"她知道如何營造氣氛——蠟燭、播放清單、氛圍。"},{"en":"The whole place had this cosy autumn vibes that I loved.","zh":"整個地方有一種我很喜歡的溫馨秋天氛圍感。"},{"en":"He curated the playlist specifically for the right vibes.","zh":"他專門為了對的氛圍感策劃了播放清單。"},{"en":"Good atmosphere does not happen by accident — it is designed.","zh":"好的氛圍感不是偶然發生的——是設計出來的。"},{"en":"This photo has such beautiful, melancholy vibes.","zh":"這張照片有一種非常美麗、憂鬱的氛圍感。"},{"en":"She said the restaurant had romantic ambiance — perfect for dates.","zh":"她說那家餐廳有浪漫的氛圍感——很適合約會。"},{"en":"I am not going there for the food — I am going for the vibes.","zh":"我去那裡不是為了食物——是為了氛圍感。"},{"en":"The golden hour light gives everything a dreamy atmosphere.","zh":"黃金時刻的光線給了一切夢幻般的氛圍感。"},{"en":"Great vibes can make ordinary moments feel extraordinary.","zh":"好的氛圍感能讓普通的時刻感覺特別。"}]},{"zh":"上頭","pinyin":"shàng tóu","en":"obsessed / hooked / going crazy over","description":"對某件事或某個人過度著迷","sentences":[{"en":"I am completely hooked on this show — watched eight episodes in a day.","zh":"我完全迷上了這部劇——一天看了八集。"},{"en":"She is obsessed with that new band — plays their songs all day.","zh":"她迷上了那個新樂隊——整天播放他們的歌曲。"},{"en":"Going crazy over someone you just met is such a feeling.","zh":"剛認識某人就這麼著迷，那種感覺太真實了。"},{"en":"I warned him not to get hooked on that game. Too late.","zh":"我警告他不要迷上那個遊戲，太遲了。"},{"en":"That dessert was so good — I am absolutely obsessed.","zh":"那個甜點太好吃了——我完全迷上了。"},{"en":"She went absolutely crazy over the new limited edition bag.","zh":"她為新款限量版包包完全瘋了。"},{"en":"Being hooked is fun until it starts affecting your sleep.","zh":"迷上某件事很有趣，直到它開始影響你的睡眠。"},{"en":"He got obsessed with cooking and now makes restaurant-quality food.","zh":"他迷上了烹飪，現在做出餐廳水準的食物。"},{"en":"I am going crazy over this artist — bought all their albums.","zh":"我瘋狂迷上了這位藝術家——買了他們所有的專輯。"},{"en":"Total obsession mode: I have watched this clip fifty times.","zh":"完全迷戀模式：我看了這個片段五十次。"}]},{"zh":"精緻窮","pinyin":"jīng zhì qióng","en":"high taste low budget / looking rich while broke","description":"生活品味要求高，但實際上沒有很多錢，精打細算地維持精緻生活","sentences":[{"en":"She is high taste low budget — thrift shops but looks like a fashion week model.","zh":"她是精緻窮——在二手店購物，但看起來像時裝週模特兒。"},{"en":"Living well on a tight budget is an art form.","zh":"在緊張預算下過好生活是一門藝術。"},{"en":"He drinks expensive coffee once a week and eats ramen the rest.","zh":"他一週喝一次貴咖啡，其餘時間吃拉麵。"},{"en":"Looking rich while actually broke is the definition of high taste low budget.","zh":"看起來有錢但實際上沒錢，就是精緻窮的定義。"},{"en":"She budgets for one luxury item a month — everything else is bargain.","zh":"她每個月預算一件奢侈品——其他一切都是划算的。"},{"en":"Being high taste low budget means knowing where to spend and where to save.","zh":"精緻窮意味著知道在哪裡花錢，在哪裡省錢。"},{"en":"He found a dupe that looks exactly like the designer bag — classic high taste low budget.","zh":"他找到了一個看起來和名牌包一模一樣的替代品——經典精緻窮。"},{"en":"The art of being high taste low budget is about priorities.","zh":"精緻窮的藝術在於優先順序的選擇。"},{"en":"She always looks put together because she shops smart, not expensive.","zh":"她看起來總是精緻，因為她聰明購物，而不是花大錢。"},{"en":"Enjoying life's small luxuries without overspending — that is the dream.","zh":"不過度消費地享受生活的小奢侈——那就是夢想。"}]},{"zh":"麻了","pinyin":"má le","en":"numb / done / speechless","description":"被某件事驚到或煩到，沒有辦法反應，完全麻木","sentences":[{"en":"My boss asked me to redo everything again. I am just numb at this point.","zh":"我的老闆又要我重做一遍。我現在已經麻了。"},{"en":"She has been waiting for two hours — totally done with everything.","zh":"她等了兩個小時——對一切都麻了。"},{"en":"Three delays in a row? I am speechless. Completely numb.","zh":"連續三次延誤？我說不出話來，完全麻了。"},{"en":"He read the email and just sat there, numb and wordless.","zh":"他讀了電子郵件，就那樣坐著，麻了說不出話。"},{"en":"I have heard so much bad news this week I am just numb.","zh":"這週我聽到了太多壞消息，我已經麻了。"},{"en":"When you are past shock and just numb — that is a whole mood.","zh":"當你超越了震驚，只是麻了——那是一種整體狀態。"},{"en":"She laughed because there was nothing else to do. Total numbness.","zh":"她笑了，因為沒有別的事可做，完全麻了。"},{"en":"Done is not defeated — sometimes numb is just processing.","zh":"麻了不是失敗——有時候麻木只是在消化。"},{"en":"He was so tired of the situation he could not even be angry anymore.","zh":"他對那個情況太厭倦了，甚至無法再生氣了。"},{"en":"Completely numb. Another deadline moved again.","zh":"完全麻了，又一個截止日期被延遲了。"}]},{"zh":"繃不住","pinyin":"běng bù zhù","en":"can't hold it together / can't keep a straight face","description":"忍不住笑，或在需要冷靜時情緒失控","sentences":[{"en":"I was trying to be serious but I just could not keep a straight face.","zh":"我試著嚴肅，但就是繃不住笑。"},{"en":"She held it together until the very end and then burst out laughing.","zh":"她一直撐著，到最後還是繃不住笑出來了。"},{"en":"I cannot hold it together watching his presentation — too funny.","zh":"看他的報告我繃不住了——太好笑了。"},{"en":"They were both trying not to laugh during the formal dinner.","zh":"他們在正式晚餐期間都努力不笑，但繃不住了。"},{"en":"He managed ten seconds of a straight face before losing it.","zh":"他保持了十秒的嚴肅，然後就繃不住了。"},{"en":"Can't keep a straight face when my friend does impressions.","zh":"當我朋友模仿別人的時候，我繃不住了。"},{"en":"I tried not to react but the look on his face made me lose it.","zh":"我試著不反應，但他臉上的表情讓我繃不住了。"},{"en":"She looked so serious trying not to laugh — everyone else cracked.","zh":"她看起來非常嚴肅地試著不笑——其他人都繃不住了。"},{"en":"Trying to hold it together in a silent meeting is a skill.","zh":"在安靜的會議中繃住是一種技能。"},{"en":"You know a joke is good when even the storyteller cannot keep a straight face.","zh":"當連說笑話的人都繃不住時，你就知道那個笑話很好笑。"}]},{"zh":"社牛","pinyin":"shè niú","en":"social butterfly / naturally social","description":"在社交場合自如、主動，和誰都能聊","sentences":[{"en":"She is a total social butterfly — walked in and knew everyone in minutes.","zh":"她是個超級社交牛人——走進去幾分鐘就和所有人都認識了。"},{"en":"He is naturally social — strangers become friends in minutes with him.","zh":"他天生就有社交能力——在他身邊，陌生人幾分鐘就成了朋友。"},{"en":"Being a social butterfly is a gift — she makes everyone feel welcome.","zh":"成為社交牛人是一種天賦——她讓所有人都感到受歡迎。"},{"en":"I wish I were more socially outgoing — it looks so effortless on her.","zh":"我希望自己更有社交能力——在她身上看起來那麼輕鬆。"},{"en":"That naturally social energy is rare — not everyone can walk into a room and own it.","zh":"那種天生的社交能量很罕見——不是每個人都能走進房間就控場。"},{"en":"She told me she used to be shy — now she is the life of the party.","zh":"她告訴我她以前很害羞——現在她是派對的靈魂人物。"},{"en":"Social butterfly mode activated — she talked to everyone at the event.","zh":"社牛模式啟動——她在活動上和每個人都說了話。"},{"en":"He struck up a conversation with a stranger and they talked for an hour.","zh":"他和一個陌生人攀談，他們聊了一個小時。"},{"en":"Her social ease makes awkward moments disappear.","zh":"她的社交自在感讓尷尬的時刻消失了。"},{"en":"Being a social butterfly takes confidence — but also genuine curiosity about people.","zh":"成為社交牛人需要自信——但也需要對人真正的好奇心。"}]},{"zh":"拿捏","pinyin":"ná niē","en":"nailed it / totally got it","description":"完全掌握某件事，表現得恰到好處","sentences":[{"en":"She nailed that presentation — every detail was perfect.","zh":"她的報告太棒了——每個細節都完美。"},{"en":"He totally got the assignment — exactly what the client wanted.","zh":"他完全掌握了那個任務——正是客戶想要的。"},{"en":"You nailed it — that outfit is perfect for the occasion.","zh":"你拿捏了——那套服裝非常適合那個場合。"},{"en":"She nailed the vibe of the event without even trying.","zh":"她毫不費力地完全掌握了活動的氛圍。"},{"en":"He always nails his characters — total commitment every time.","zh":"他每次都完美詮釋他的角色——每次都全力投入。"},{"en":"I finally nailed the recipe after ten failed attempts.","zh":"在十次失敗嘗試後，我終於拿捏了這個食譜。"},{"en":"She nailed the interview and got an offer on the spot.","zh":"她面試表現完美，當場收到了錄取通知。"},{"en":"Nailing the right tone in an email is harder than it sounds.","zh":"在電子郵件中拿捏正確的語氣比聽起來難多了。"},{"en":"He nailed it — landed the project on time and under budget.","zh":"他拿捏了——按時且在預算內完成了項目。"},{"en":"When she sings that high note, she nails it every single time.","zh":"當她唱那個高音時，她每次都完美拿捏。"}]},{"zh":"種草","pinyin":"zhòng cǎo","en":"recommend / inspire to buy / make someone want something","description":"讓別人對某件事產生興趣或購買慾","sentences":[{"en":"She recommended that skincare brand and now I cannot stop thinking about it.","zh":"她推薦了那個護膚品牌，現在我腦海中一直在想它。"},{"en":"His review completely inspired me to buy — I ordered it immediately.","zh":"他的評論完全讓我有了購買的衝動——我立刻訂購了。"},{"en":"She is a walking recommendation engine — she inspires me to buy everything.","zh":"她是一個行走的推薦機器——她讓我想買一切。"},{"en":"That travel content made me want to go immediately.","zh":"那個旅遊內容讓我立刻想去了。"},{"en":"I got inspired to buy that book from a thirty-second video.","zh":"我從一個三十秒的視頻中被種草了那本書。"},{"en":"Her food content inspires me every single time.","zh":"她的美食內容每次都讓我種草。"},{"en":"The way she talked about that café made everyone want to go.","zh":"她談論那家咖啡廳的方式讓所有人都想去了。"},{"en":"He posts recommendations that genuinely make you want things.","zh":"他發布的推薦真的讓你想要那些東西。"},{"en":"That one photo inspired me to buy the exact same outfit.","zh":"那一張照片讓我種草了完全相同的服裝。"},{"en":"Good content inspires without feeling like an ad.","zh":"好的內容讓你種草，但不感覺像廣告。"}]},{"zh":"搭子","pinyin":"dā zi","en":"partner / go-to person / companion","description":"在特定活動中的固定同伴，可以是吃飯搭子、旅遊搭子等","sentences":[{"en":"I need a travel companion for this trip — anyone interested?","zh":"我需要一個旅遊搭子——有人感興趣嗎？"},{"en":"She is my go-to person for trying new restaurants.","zh":"她是我嘗試新餐廳的固定搭子。"},{"en":"We became gym partners and now we both actually show up.","zh":"我們成了健身搭子，現在我們兩個都真的去了。"},{"en":"Having a study companion keeps you accountable.","zh":"有一個學習搭子讓你保持自律。"},{"en":"He is my perfect shopping partner — same taste, same budget.","zh":"他是我完美的購物搭子——相同的品味，相同的預算。"},{"en":"Finding a coffee companion who does not mind sitting for hours is rare.","zh":"找到一個不介意坐上幾個小時的咖啡搭子是很難得的。"},{"en":"She is my hiking companion every single weekend.","zh":"她是我每個週末的登山搭子。"},{"en":"I met my closest friend as a commute companion — same train every day.","zh":"我遇到我最親密的朋友是作為通勤搭子——每天同一班列車。"},{"en":"We are perfect partners in crime for any food adventure.","zh":"我們是任何美食探索的完美搭子。"},{"en":"Good companions make any activity more fun.","zh":"好的搭子讓任何活動都更有趣。"}]},{"zh":"嘴替","pinyin":"zuǐ tì","en":"speaks for me / mouthpiece / says what I cannot","description":"說出了你心裡話的人或內容","sentences":[{"en":"She said exactly what I was thinking — total mouthpiece moment.","zh":"她說出了我心裡想的——完全是嘴替時刻。"},{"en":"That comment speaks for me — I could not have said it better.","zh":"那個評論說出了我的心聲——我說不出更好的了。"},{"en":"He is my mouthpiece in meetings — says what I am too scared to say.","zh":"他是我在會議中的嘴替——說了我太害怕說的話。"},{"en":"That comedian speaks for an entire generation of burnt-out workers.","zh":"那個喜劇演員是整整一代倦怠工人的嘴替。"},{"en":"This song is my mouthpiece — every lyric hits.","zh":"這首歌是我的嘴替——每一句歌詞都說到心坎了。"},{"en":"She is my mouthpiece with my family — says the things I cannot.","zh":"她是我面對家人的嘴替——說了我無法說的話。"},{"en":"That tweet speaks for millions of people who feel the same.","zh":"那條推文是數百萬有同感的人的嘴替。"},{"en":"Finding a friend who speaks for you when you are frozen is priceless.","zh":"找到一個在你冰住時為你說話的朋友是無價的。"},{"en":"Her book is a mouthpiece for everyone who has ever felt invisible.","zh":"她的書是所有曾感到被忽視的人的嘴替。"},{"en":"He always speaks for me in awkward situations — I owe him.","zh":"他總是在尷尬的情況下為我說話——我欠他的。"}]},{"zh":"報復性熬夜","pinyin":"bào fù xìng áo yè","en":"revenge bedtime procrastination","description":"白天沒有自己的時間，所以故意熬夜來補回屬於自己的時光","sentences":[{"en":"I do revenge bedtime procrastination — the only time I have to myself is 1am.","zh":"我做報復性熬夜——唯一屬於我自己的時間是凌晨一點。"},{"en":"After a long day of work, she stays up late just to feel some freedom.","zh":"工作了漫長的一天後，她熬夜只是為了感受一點自由。"},{"en":"Revenge bedtime procrastination is when you refuse to sleep because you need me-time.","zh":"報復性熬夜是當你拒絕睡覺，因為你需要屬於自己的時間。"},{"en":"He knows it is bad but scrolling at midnight is the only peace he gets.","zh":"他知道這樣不好，但午夜刷手機是他得到的唯一平靜。"},{"en":"My therapist explained my late-night habits as a form of taking back control.","zh":"我的治療師解釋我的熬夜習慣是一種奪回控制的方式。"},{"en":"She stays up until 2am just to read — quiet time she cannot find during the day.","zh":"她熬夜到凌晨兩點只是為了讀書——白天找不到的安靜時間。"},{"en":"Revenge bedtime procrastination is exhausting and yet so hard to quit.","zh":"報復性熬夜很令人疲憊，但又很難戒掉。"},{"en":"The cure is creating daytime moments of rest and joy — hard but necessary.","zh":"解決方法是在白天創造休息和快樂的時刻——很難，但很必要。"},{"en":"I know I need sleep. I also know I need this one hour of silence.","zh":"我知道我需要睡眠，我也知道我需要這一小時的安靜。"},{"en":"Night owls are not all lazy — some are just reclaiming their time.","zh":"夜貓子並不都是懶惰的——有些只是在奪回自己的時間。"}]},{"zh":"電子榨菜","pinyin":"diàn zǐ zhà cài","en":"background media / mindless content","description":"吃飯或做事時放著看的輕鬆無腦的影片或節目","sentences":[{"en":"I always have background media playing when I eat — usually a reality show.","zh":"我吃飯時總是播放背景媒體——通常是真人秀。"},{"en":"That show is pure mindless content — perfect for dinner.","zh":"那個節目是純粹的電子榨菜——非常適合吃晚飯時看。"},{"en":"She cannot eat alone without something playing in the background.","zh":"她不能獨自吃飯，沒有什麼在背景播放。"},{"en":"Mindless content is not bad — it is sometimes exactly what you need.","zh":"電子榨菜不壞——有時候這正是你需要的。"},{"en":"I have rewatched that show five times — ultimate background media.","zh":"我重看了那個節目五次——終極電子榨菜。"},{"en":"He plays podcasts as mindless background while doing household chores.","zh":"他在做家務時播放播客作為電子榨菜。"},{"en":"Low-effort, comfortable content — that is what background media is.","zh":"低努力、舒適的內容——那就是電子榨菜。"},{"en":"She discovered that cooking shows are perfect dinner background media.","zh":"她發現烹飪節目是完美的吃飯電子榨菜。"},{"en":"Sometimes you do not want to think — background content is okay.","zh":"有時候你不想思考——電子榨菜沒問題。"},{"en":"Good background media is always running in a corner of my screen.","zh":"好的電子榨菜總是在我螢幕的一個角落播放著。"}]},{"zh":"顯眼包","pinyin":"xiǎn yǎn bāo","en":"attention seeker / show-off / stands out","description":"特別引人注意的人或物，可以是正面也可以是負面","sentences":[{"en":"She walked in wearing the brightest outfit — total attention seeker.","zh":"她穿著最亮眼的服裝走進來——完全是顯眼包。"},{"en":"He is such a show-off but in the most loveable way.","zh":"他是個顯眼包，但以最可愛的方式。"},{"en":"That bright yellow bag is such a statement piece — it stands out everywhere.","zh":"那個亮黃色的包是如此搶眼——在任何地方都很顯眼。"},{"en":"She is the kind of person who stands out without trying.","zh":"她是那種不費力就脫穎而出的人。"},{"en":"His car is so loud — such an attention-seeker move.","zh":"他的車太吵了——完全是顯眼包行為。"},{"en":"Being a show-off is fine when the talent backs it up.","zh":"當才能支撐得住時，做顯眼包沒問題。"},{"en":"She wore bright red to the all-grey event — pure attention seeker.","zh":"她在一片灰色的活動上穿了鮮紅色——純粹的顯眼包。"},{"en":"That building is the attention seeker of the whole neighbourhood.","zh":"那棟建築是整個社區的顯眼包。"},{"en":"Being the centre of attention comes naturally to her.","zh":"成為注意力中心對她來說很自然。"},{"en":"He did not mean to stand out — he just naturally attracts eyes.","zh":"他不是故意要脫穎而出——他只是天然地吸引目光。"}]},{"zh":"後勁很大","pinyin":"hòu jìn hěn dà","en":"hits harder later / slow burn","description":"一件事或一部作品，起初不覺得如何，後來越想越有感","sentences":[{"en":"That ending had such a slow burn effect — I cried on the train home.","zh":"那個結局有一種慢燃效果——我在回家的地鐵上哭了。"},{"en":"The film was okay at the time but it hit harder on the walk home.","zh":"那部電影當時感覺還好，但在回家的路上越想越有感。"},{"en":"Some songs hit harder after a few listens — delayed impact.","zh":"有些歌曲多聽幾遍後越來越有感——後勁很大。"},{"en":"That advice did not make sense until three years later.","zh":"那個建議直到三年後才讓我明白。"},{"en":"The more you think about the lyrics, the harder it hits.","zh":"你越想那些歌詞，後勁就越大。"},{"en":"This photo hits harder every time I look at it.","zh":"這張照片每次看都越來越有感。"},{"en":"She did not cry during the movie — but later, alone, the slow burn hit.","zh":"她在電影中沒哭——但後來，獨自一人時，後勁到了。"},{"en":"Books with slow burn impact are the ones that change you.","zh":"有後勁的書才是真正改變你的書。"},{"en":"That speech had delayed impact — I did not grasp it until the next day.","zh":"那個演講後勁很大——我到第二天才真正理解它。"},{"en":"The slow burn feeling is often a sign of something truly great.","zh":"後勁大的感覺往往是真正偉大的事物的標誌。"}]},{"zh":"共情","pinyin":"gòng qíng","en":"empathy / resonating with","description":"感同身受，理解並分享他人的情感","sentences":[{"en":"I felt so much empathy reading her story — it resonated deeply.","zh":"讀到她的故事，我感同身受——深深地產生了共鳴。"},{"en":"She has a gift for empathy — she makes everyone feel understood.","zh":"她有共情的天賦——讓每個人都感到被理解。"},{"en":"That post resonated with millions because it spoke a shared truth.","zh":"那篇文章與數百萬人共情，因為它說出了共同的真相。"},{"en":"Good storytelling creates empathy between strangers.","zh":"好的敘事在陌生人之間產生共情。"},{"en":"He understood without me having to explain — pure empathy.","zh":"他不需要我解釋就明白了——純粹的共情。"},{"en":"Empathy is listening to understand, not just to respond.","zh":"共情是為了理解而傾聽，而不只是為了回應。"},{"en":"I resonated with every word of that song — like it was written for me.","zh":"我和那首歌的每一個詞都共情了——好像是為我寫的。"},{"en":"She builds empathy through her stories — readers feel everything.","zh":"她通過她的故事建立共情——讀者感受到一切。"},{"en":"Truly resonating with someone takes vulnerability.","zh":"真正與某人共情需要脆弱。"},{"en":"That documentary made me empathise with people I never understood before.","zh":"那部紀錄片讓我與以前從未理解過的人共情了。"}]},{"zh":"整頓職場","pinyin":"zhěng dùn zhí chǎng","en":"setting the workplace straight / workplace reform","description":"年輕員工不再忍氣吞聲，勇於說出問題，改變不良職場文化","sentences":[{"en":"She refused to do unpaid overtime and set the whole department straight.","zh":"她拒絕做無薪加班，整頓了整個部門。"},{"en":"The new generation is reforming workplace culture — and it is about time.","zh":"新一代正在改革職場文化——早就該這樣了。"},{"en":"He called out the toxic meeting culture and actually changed it.","zh":"他指出了有毒的會議文化，並真正改變了它。"},{"en":"Setting the workplace straight is uncomfortable but necessary.","zh":"整頓職場是不舒服的，但很必要。"},{"en":"She is one employee who would not tolerate disrespect — and people noticed.","zh":"她是一個不容忍不尊重的員工——大家都注意到了。"},{"en":"Workplace reform starts with one person being brave enough to speak up.","zh":"職場改革從一個人夠勇敢說出來開始。"},{"en":"He documented every violation and presented it calmly to HR.","zh":"他記錄了每一次違規行為，並冷靜地向人力資源部提出。"},{"en":"She set the record straight in the meeting — no more free labour.","zh":"她在會議中整頓了局面——不再有免費勞動力。"},{"en":"Young workers demanding respect is workplace reform in action.","zh":"年輕員工要求尊重是職場整頓的實際行動。"},{"en":"Calling out bad management is not rebellion — it is reform.","zh":"指出糟糕的管理不是叛逆——而是整頓。"}]},{"zh":"社死","pinyin":"shè sǐ","en":"social death / mortifying moment","description":"當眾出糗，極度尷尬想消失的時刻","sentences":[{"en":"I waved back at someone who was not waving at me. Total social death.","zh":"我向一個沒有向我揮手的人揮手，完全社死了。"},{"en":"She called her teacher 'mum' in front of the whole class — social death.","zh":"她在全班面前叫老師「媽媽」——社死了。"},{"en":"Walking into the wrong meeting room and not realising for five minutes — pure mortification.","zh":"走進了錯誤的會議室，五分鐘後才發現——完全社死。"},{"en":"I sent the text to the wrong person. The person it was about. Social death.","zh":"我把訊息發給了錯誤的人，就是我說的那個人——社死了。"},{"en":"She pronounced the French word wrong in front of native speakers. Mortifying.","zh":"她在母語人士面前把法語單詞念錯了，太社死了。"},{"en":"Slipping in front of a crowd and everyone turning to look — social death.","zh":"在人群中滑倒，所有人都轉頭看——社死了。"},{"en":"He told the same story twice to the same person. Immediate social death.","zh":"他對同一個人講了同一個故事兩次，立刻社死。"},{"en":"I laughed at a joke I did not hear just to fit in. Mortifying.","zh":"我為了合群笑了一個我沒聽到的笑話，太社死了。"},{"en":"We have all had a social death moment — you survive it.","zh":"我們都有過社死的時刻——你會活下去的。"},{"en":"She handled her social death moment with grace and a good story.","zh":"她用優雅和好笑的方式處理了她社死的時刻。"}]},{"zh":"發瘋","pinyin":"fā fēng","en":"going unhinged / losing it / chaotic energy","description":"情緒崩潰或故意用誇張、無厘頭的方式表達情緒","sentences":[{"en":"I have been awake for twenty hours. I am fully going unhinged.","zh":"我已經清醒了二十個小時，我完全在發瘋了。"},{"en":"She started talking to her plants — full chaotic energy.","zh":"她開始和她的植物說話——完全發瘋的能量。"},{"en":"He sent a wall of chaotic text at 3am. Going unhinged.","zh":"他在凌晨三點發了一段混亂的長文，完全在發瘋。"},{"en":"I am about to lose it — everything is due tomorrow.","zh":"我快要發瘋了——所有東西都是明天截止。"},{"en":"When everything goes wrong at once, unhinged energy is the only response.","zh":"當所有事情同時出錯，發瘋的能量是唯一的回應。"},{"en":"She went full chaos mode and somehow fixed the problem.","zh":"她進入完全發瘋模式，但不知為何解決了問題。"},{"en":"My brain is going unhinged — I cannot focus on anything.","zh":"我的大腦在發瘋——我無法專注於任何事情。"},{"en":"That message was pure unhinged energy and I loved it.","zh":"那條訊息完全是發瘋的能量，我很喜歡。"},{"en":"Chaotic people get things done in unexpected ways.","zh":"發瘋的人以意想不到的方式完成事情。"},{"en":"Sometimes the only sane response to an insane situation is to go unhinged.","zh":"有時候，對瘋狂情況唯一理智的回應就是發瘋。"}]},{"zh":"卷王","pinyin":"juǎn wáng","en":"top hustler / overachiever / king of the rat race","description":"在內捲競爭中表現最瘋狂、努力最多的人","sentences":[{"en":"He is the top hustler in the office — first in, last out every single day.","zh":"他是辦公室裡最捲的人——每天第一個到，最後一個走。"},{"en":"She is the overachiever everyone competes against — and always loses to.","zh":"她是大家都在競爭的卷王——但總是輸給她。"},{"en":"He pulls all-nighters just to stay ahead — classic hustler mentality.","zh":"他為了保持領先而通宵——典型的卷王心態。"},{"en":"Being the top hustler might get you recognition but at what cost?","zh":"成為卷王可能讓你獲得認可，但代價是什麼？"},{"en":"She does not compete to win — she just loves doing more than everyone.","zh":"她不是為了贏才競爭——她只是喜歡比別人做更多。"},{"en":"The overachiever is rarely the happiest person in the room.","zh":"卷王很少是房間裡最快樂的人。"},{"en":"He hustled so hard he forgot why he started in the first place.","zh":"他太拼了，以至於忘記了他最初為什麼開始。"},{"en":"Being a top hustler is admired until you burn out.","zh":"成為卷王讓人欽佩，直到你倦怠。"},{"en":"She stepped back from being the overachiever and felt so much lighter.","zh":"她從卷王的位置退下來，感覺輕鬆多了。"},{"en":"Some overachievers are running from something — not toward something.","zh":"一些卷王是在逃離某些事情——而不是追向某些事情。"}]},{"zh":"出圈","pinyin":"chū quān","en":"going mainstream / crossing over / going viral","description":"從小眾圈子突破到廣大大眾的關注","sentences":[{"en":"That song went from niche to mainstream overnight.","zh":"那首歌一夜之間從小眾走向了主流。"},{"en":"She crossed over from the gaming community to a general audience.","zh":"她從遊戲社群跨越到了普通大眾。"},{"en":"His cooking videos went viral and now he has millions of followers.","zh":"他的烹飪視頻爆紅，現在有數百萬粉絲。"},{"en":"That meme crossed over from one community to everyone's feed.","zh":"那個梗從一個社群擴散到所有人的動態。"},{"en":"She went mainstream after one feature in a major publication.","zh":"她在一家大型媒體的一篇報道後走向了主流。"},{"en":"Going viral changes things — suddenly everyone knows your name.","zh":"爆紅改變了一切——突然間所有人都知道你的名字。"},{"en":"He never expected his art to go mainstream — it just happened.","zh":"他從沒想到他的藝術會走向主流——它就這樣發生了。"},{"en":"Crossing over from local fame to national fame is a big leap.","zh":"從地方知名度跨越到全國知名度是一個很大的跳躍。"},{"en":"The series went mainstream when a celebrity mentioned it online.","zh":"這個系列在一位名人在網上提到它後走向了主流。"},{"en":"Going mainstream does not always mean selling out.","zh":"走向主流並不總是意味著出賣自己。"}]},{"zh":"爆款","pinyin":"bào kuǎn","en":"viral hit / bestseller / hot item","description":"迅速走紅、大賣的商品或內容","sentences":[{"en":"That video became a viral hit overnight — twenty million views.","zh":"那個視頻一夜之間成了爆款——兩千萬次觀看。"},{"en":"She released a bestseller that no one expected to do so well.","zh":"她發布了一本沒人預料會這麼好賣的暢銷書。"},{"en":"That product became a hot item after one review from a top influencer.","zh":"那個產品在一位頂級網紅評論後成了爆款。"},{"en":"The viral hit formula is impossible to predict — it just happens.","zh":"爆款的公式是無法預測的——它就是會發生。"},{"en":"She creates content hoping for a viral hit, knowing it is unpredictable.","zh":"她創作內容希望成為爆款，但知道這是不可預測的。"},{"en":"That café became a hot spot after going viral on social media.","zh":"那家咖啡廳在社交媒體上爆紅後成了熱門地點。"},{"en":"A bestselling product solves a real problem people did not know they had.","zh":"一個爆款產品解決了人們不知道自己有的真實問題。"},{"en":"He made a viral hit by accident — now he cannot replicate it.","zh":"他意外地做出了爆款——現在他無法複製它。"},{"en":"Going viral is exciting until you have to manage the attention.","zh":"爆紅是令人興奮的，直到你不得不管理那些關注。"},{"en":"The hot item sold out in minutes — she missed it again.","zh":"爆款在幾分鐘內就賣完了——她又錯過了。"}]},{"zh":"帶貨","pinyin":"dài huò","en":"selling through influence / product placement","description":"通過推薦讓粉絲購買產品，影響消費行為","sentences":[{"en":"She sells products through her influence — one post moves thousands of units.","zh":"她通過影響力銷售產品——一篇文章能賣出數千件。"},{"en":"Product placement has become more natural — it blends into content.","zh":"帶貨變得更自然了——它融入了內容中。"},{"en":"He reviews genuinely — he only promotes things he actually uses.","zh":"他真誠地評測——他只推廣他真正使用的東西。"},{"en":"Influencer marketing is effective because it feels like a recommendation from a friend.","zh":"帶貨行銷有效，因為它感覺像是朋友的推薦。"},{"en":"She drove so much traffic to that brand they had to restock three times.","zh":"她為那個品牌帶來了大量流量，他們不得不補貨三次。"},{"en":"The line between genuine review and paid promotion is blurry.","zh":"真實評測和付費推廣之間的界限很模糊。"},{"en":"He turned his hobby into a business by selling through his platform.","zh":"他通過他的平台帶貨，把愛好變成了生意。"},{"en":"Selling through influence works when the audience trusts you.","zh":"帶貨在觀眾信任你的時候才有效。"},{"en":"She disclosed her sponsorship openly — transparency matters.","zh":"她公開披露了她的贊助——透明度很重要。"},{"en":"The best influencer marketing does not feel like marketing at all.","zh":"最好的帶貨感覺根本不像行銷。"}]},{"zh":"打卡","pinyin":"dǎ kǎ","en":"checking in / documenting a visit / stamp collecting","description":"到某個地方打個卡，拍照記錄，完成儀式感","sentences":[{"en":"She checked in at every landmark on the trip — full documentation mode.","zh":"她在旅途中每個地標都打了卡——完全的記錄模式。"},{"en":"He checks in at every café he visits — his grid is a travel diary.","zh":"他在每家訪問的咖啡廳都打卡——他的動態是一本旅遊日記。"},{"en":"I check in at the gym daily — accountability through social media.","zh":"我每天在健身房打卡——通過社交媒體保持自律。"},{"en":"Documenting every experience is fine until you forget to just be present.","zh":"記錄每一個體驗是好的，直到你忘記只是活在當下。"},{"en":"She ticked off every item on her café list — a full checking-in tour.","zh":"她完成了她咖啡廳清單上的每一項——一個完整的打卡之旅。"},{"en":"The new exhibit had people queuing just to check in for the photo.","zh":"新展覽讓人們排隊只是為了打卡拍照。"},{"en":"Checking in is fun but I try to enjoy the place first, then document.","zh":"打卡很有趣，但我試著先享受這個地方，再記錄。"},{"en":"He built a following just by checking in at interesting places.","zh":"他只是通過打卡有趣的地方就積累了一批粉絲。"},{"en":"Some people travel to check in. Others check in because they travel.","zh":"有些人旅行是為了打卡，另一些人打卡是因為他們在旅行。"},{"en":"Her check-in posts inspired me to visit places I never considered.","zh":"她的打卡帖子讓我受到啟發，去了我從未考慮過的地方。"}]},{"zh":"人設崩塌","pinyin":"rén shè bēng tā","en":"image collapse / persona destroyed","description":"某人精心維護的公眾形象突然因事件而崩潰","sentences":[{"en":"His carefully crafted persona collapsed after the leaked messages.","zh":"在洩露的訊息之後，他精心打造的形象崩塌了。"},{"en":"The image collapse happened quickly — one video undid years of branding.","zh":"形象崩塌發生得很快——一個視頻摧毀了多年的品牌建設。"},{"en":"She had a perfect persona until the truth came out.","zh":"她有一個完美的人設，直到真相曝光。"},{"en":"The persona collapsed and surprisingly, people liked the real version more.","zh":"人設崩塌了，令人驚訝的是，人們更喜歡真實的版本。"},{"en":"Building a persona on lies is risky — the collapse is inevitable.","zh":"建立在謊言上的人設是危險的——崩塌是不可避免的。"},{"en":"Her image collapse became the biggest story of the year.","zh":"她的人設崩塌成了那年最大的新聞。"},{"en":"He rebuilt after the persona collapse — more honest this time.","zh":"他在人設崩塌後重建了——這次更誠實。"},{"en":"Audiences actually appreciate authenticity over a perfect persona.","zh":"觀眾實際上欣賞真實性，而不是完美的人設。"},{"en":"The image collapse taught him that pretending is exhausting.","zh":"人設崩塌讓他意識到裝扮是很累的。"},{"en":"She never built a persona — so there was nothing to collapse.","zh":"她從來沒有建立人設——所以沒有什麼可以崩塌的。"}]},{"zh":"蹭熱度","pinyin":"cèng rè dù","en":"clout chasing / jumping on trends","description":"利用他人或熱點話題的熱度來為自己增加曝光","sentences":[{"en":"He commented on every viral post to ride the clout wave.","zh":"他對每個爆紅帖子都評論，蹭熱度。"},{"en":"She jumped on every trend whether it suited her brand or not.","zh":"她不管趨勢是否適合她的品牌，都跟風蹭熱度。"},{"en":"Clout chasing is obvious and audiences can tell.","zh":"蹭熱度很明顯，觀眾能看出來。"},{"en":"Some clout chasing works — but most looks desperate.","zh":"一些蹭熱度的行為有效——但大多數看起來很絕望。"},{"en":"He rode the viral trend and gained ten thousand followers overnight.","zh":"他蹭了那個爆紅趨勢，一夜之間獲得了一萬個粉絲。"},{"en":"Jumping on trends only works if you genuinely fit the conversation.","zh":"蹭熱度只有在你真正適合那個話題時才有效。"},{"en":"She refused to jump on tragedy trends — principles over clout.","zh":"她拒絕蹭悲劇熱度——原則高於熱度。"},{"en":"Clout chasing can damage a brand if it feels forced.","zh":"如果感覺很強迫，蹭熱度可能會損害品牌。"},{"en":"He built genuine influence instead of chasing clout.","zh":"他建立了真正的影響力，而不是蹭熱度。"},{"en":"The best way to stay relevant is to be genuine, not to chase trends.","zh":"保持相關性的最佳方式是真實，而不是追趨勢。"}]},{"zh":"躺贏","pinyin":"tǎng yíng","en":"winning effortlessly / accidental success","description":"不費力氣卻獲得成功，撿到便宜","sentences":[{"en":"She entered the contest as a joke and won first place — pure effortless winning.","zh":"她把參賽當成玩笑，卻贏得了第一名——純粹的躺贏。"},{"en":"He forgot to cancel his subscription and got a refund plus free months — total accidental success.","zh":"他忘記取消訂閱，卻得到了退款加上免費月份——完全躺贏。"},{"en":"Winning effortlessly sounds great until you feel guilty about it.","zh":"躺贏聽起來很好，直到你對此感到愧疚。"},{"en":"She networked for years and then got the opportunity out of nowhere.","zh":"她多年來建立人脈，然後機會不知從哪裡來了。"},{"en":"Sometimes luck is an effortless win — take it and be grateful.","zh":"有時候運氣就是躺贏——接受它並感恩。"},{"en":"He stumbled into the right room at the right time — accidental success.","zh":"他在正確的時間走進了正確的房間——躺贏了。"},{"en":"Effortless wins exist but they are often built on invisible work.","zh":"躺贏存在，但它們通常建立在看不見的努力上。"},{"en":"She landed the deal without even trying — right place, right time.","zh":"她甚至沒有努力就談成了那筆交易——天時地利。"},{"en":"Accidental success is a real thing — but preparation meets opportunity.","zh":"躺贏是真實存在的——但機遇總是遇上有準備的人。"},{"en":"He always seems to win effortlessly but no one sees the preparation behind it.","zh":"他看起來總是躺贏，但沒有人看到背後的準備。"}]},{"zh":"直球","pinyin":"zhí qiú","en":"being direct / straight to the point","description":"不拐彎抹角，直接說出想法或感受","sentences":[{"en":"She asked him out directly — no hints, no games, just a direct question.","zh":"她直接問他出去——沒有暗示，沒有遊戲，就是一個直接的問題。"},{"en":"He sent a direct text: 'I like you. Do you want to go on a date?'","zh":"他發了一條直球訊息：「我喜歡你，你想去約會嗎？」"},{"en":"Being direct saves so much time and misunderstanding.","zh":"直球表達節省了很多時間和誤解。"},{"en":"She is famous for her directness — people appreciate the honesty.","zh":"她以直球表達著稱——人們欣賞這種誠實。"},{"en":"I am going to be straight to the point: I want a raise.","zh":"我要直球說：我想加薪。"},{"en":"Direct communication is a skill — not everyone can do it without being rude.","zh":"直球溝通是一種技能——不是每個人都能做到不失禮貌。"},{"en":"He went straight to the point and everyone respected him for it.","zh":"他直球表達，所有人都因此尊重他。"},{"en":"Being direct about feelings is terrifying but so much better than hints.","zh":"直球表達感受是可怕的，但比暗示要好得多。"},{"en":"She cut the small talk and got straight to business — I loved that.","zh":"她省略了閒聊，直接進入正題——我很喜歡那樣。"},{"en":"Direct does not mean harsh. You can be kind and still be straight.","zh":"直球不意味著嚴厲，你可以既善良又直接。"}]},{"zh":"走心","pinyin":"zǒu xīn","en":"heartfelt / putting in genuine effort","description":"用心做某件事，情感真誠投入","sentences":[{"en":"That apology was so heartfelt — you could feel he meant every word.","zh":"那個道歉非常走心——你能感覺到他每個字都是認真的。"},{"en":"She puts genuine effort into every gift — always the most thoughtful one.","zh":"她在每份禮物上都很走心——總是最用心的那個。"},{"en":"A heartfelt message is worth more than an expensive gift.","zh":"一條走心的訊息比昂貴的禮物更有價值。"},{"en":"He wrote her a letter by hand — totally heartfelt and unexpected.","zh":"他手寫了一封信給她——完全走心，出乎意料。"},{"en":"That speech had genuine effort behind it — everyone was moved.","zh":"那篇演講背後有真誠的付出——每個人都被感動了。"},{"en":"Putting in genuine effort is rare and always appreciated.","zh":"走心是稀少的，永遠都會被欣賞。"},{"en":"She made a playlist specifically for him — heartfelt and personal.","zh":"她專門為他制作了一個播放清單——走心而個人化。"},{"en":"Heartfelt work stands out in a world of half-hearted efforts.","zh":"在一個敷衍了事的世界裡，走心的作品會脫穎而出。"},{"en":"He put genuine effort into learning her language for their trip.","zh":"他在他們的旅行中用心學習了她的語言。"},{"en":"The most meaningful things in life are usually the most heartfelt.","zh":"生活中最有意義的事情通常是最走心的。"}]},{"zh":"情緒價值","pinyin":"qíng xù jià zhí","en":"emotional value / makes you feel good","description":"某事物提供的情感滿足感，讓人感到快樂、安慰或滿足","sentences":[{"en":"She bought the expensive candle purely for emotional value — it made her happy.","zh":"她買那根貴蠟燭純粹是為了情緒價值——它讓她快樂。"},{"en":"Some things are not practical but they have emotional value — that matters.","zh":"有些東西不實用，但有情緒價值——這很重要。"},{"en":"He gives great emotional value as a friend — always makes you feel seen.","zh":"他作為朋友提供了很好的情緒價值——總是讓你感到被看見。"},{"en":"That coffee shop has emotional value beyond the coffee itself.","zh":"那家咖啡廳有超越咖啡本身的情緒價值。"},{"en":"Emotional value is why we keep things that serve no practical purpose.","zh":"情緒價值是我們保留沒有實際用途的東西的原因。"},{"en":"She fills every space with things that have emotional value — her home shows it.","zh":"她用有情緒價值的東西填滿每個空間——她的家就能看出來。"},{"en":"A product that makes you feel something is worth more than one that just works.","zh":"能讓你有感覺的產品比單純好用的產品更有價值。"},{"en":"He understands emotional value — that is why his gifts are always perfect.","zh":"他理解情緒價值——這就是為什麼他的禮物總是完美的。"},{"en":"Music, art, and stories have emotional value that logic cannot measure.","zh":"音樂、藝術和故事有情緒價值，邏輯無法衡量。"},{"en":"Emotional value is underrated in a world obsessed with practicality.","zh":"在一個沉迷於實用性的世界裡，情緒價值被低估了。"}]},{"zh":"鬆弛感","pinyin":"sōng chí gǎn","en":"relaxed energy / effortless ease","description":"一種自然輕鬆、不費力、不焦慮的生活狀態或氣質","sentences":[{"en":"She carries this relaxed energy that makes everyone around her calm down.","zh":"她帶著一種讓周圍所有人都平靜下來的鬆弛感。"},{"en":"He has effortless ease — nothing seems to stress him out.","zh":"他有一種毫不費力的從容——沒有什麼能讓他有壓力。"},{"en":"That effortless, relaxed energy is so magnetic to be around.","zh":"那種輕鬆自在的鬆弛感非常有吸引力。"},{"en":"Relaxed energy is not laziness — it is peace under pressure.","zh":"鬆弛感不是懶惰——而是在壓力下的平靜。"},{"en":"Her whole vibe is effortless ease — like she has figured it all out.","zh":"她整個氛圍都是鬆弛感——好像她已經搞清楚了一切。"},{"en":"I am trying to cultivate a more relaxed energy — stop reacting to everything.","zh":"我在努力培養更多的鬆弛感——停止對每件事都做出反應。"},{"en":"The most attractive quality is genuine ease in your own skin.","zh":"最有吸引力的特質是在自己皮膚裡的真正鬆弛感。"},{"en":"He walks into rooms with effortless ease and people notice.","zh":"他帶著鬆弛感走進房間，人們都會注意到。"},{"en":"Relaxed energy is contagious — one calm person can change a whole room.","zh":"鬆弛感是有感染力的——一個冷靜的人能改變整個房間的氛圍。"},{"en":"She is not trying to impress anyone — pure effortless ease.","zh":"她不是在試圖給任何人留下深刻印象——純粹的鬆弛感。"}]},{"zh":"精神內耗","pinyin":"jīng shén nèi hào","en":"mental drain / internal mental exhaustion","description":"內心不停地自我懷疑、反覆糾結、消耗大量心理能量","sentences":[{"en":"I spent three hours in mental drain over a decision I made two years ago.","zh":"我花了三個小時在兩年前做的決定上精神內耗。"},{"en":"She is exhausting herself mentally — overthinking every small thing.","zh":"她在精神上耗盡自己——對每件小事都過度思考。"},{"en":"Internal mental exhaustion from replaying conversations is real.","zh":"反覆回放對話帶來的精神內耗是真實的。"},{"en":"He drains himself mentally worrying about things that never happen.","zh":"他因為擔心永遠不會發生的事情而精神內耗。"},{"en":"Mental drain from indecision is just as tiring as physical work.","zh":"因優柔寡斷而精神內耗，和體力工作一樣令人疲憊。"},{"en":"I am trying to reduce mental drain by just making decisions and moving on.","zh":"我試著通過快速做決定並繼續前進來減少精神內耗。"},{"en":"She realised her anxiety was mostly internal mental exhaustion, not real danger.","zh":"她意識到她的焦慮主要是精神內耗，而不是真正的危險。"},{"en":"Mental drain from social comparison is one of the biggest energy thieves.","zh":"因社交比較而產生的精神內耗是最大的能量小偷之一。"},{"en":"The cure for mental drain is often action — stop thinking, start doing.","zh":"精神內耗的解藥往往是行動——停止思考，開始行動。"},{"en":"He stopped the mental drain by journalling every worry out of his head.","zh":"他通過把每個擔憂寫進日記來停止精神內耗。"}]},{"zh":"治癒系","pinyin":"zhì yù xì","en":"healing / soothing / feel-good content","description":"能讓人感到治癒、溫暖、舒緩情緒的事物或內容","sentences":[{"en":"That video of puppies is pure healing content — I watch it when stressed.","zh":"那個小狗的視頻是純粹的治癒系內容——我壓力大時就看。"},{"en":"She creates soothing content — slow-paced, gentle, and genuinely calming.","zh":"她創作治癒系內容——節奏緩慢、輕柔、真的很平靜。"},{"en":"His voice has healing energy — listening to him talk calms me down.","zh":"他的聲音有治癒的能量——聽他說話讓我平靜。"},{"en":"Feel-good content is what the internet was made for.","zh":"治癒系內容是網路存在的意義。"},{"en":"She decorated her home with soothing, healing elements.","zh":"她用治癒系的元素裝飾了她的家。"},{"en":"That anime has pure healing energy — nothing bad ever happens.","zh":"那部動漫有純粹的治癒系能量——沒有任何壞事發生。"},{"en":"I need some healing content tonight — it has been a hard week.","zh":"我今晚需要一些治癒系的內容——這週很辛苦。"},{"en":"His photography has a healing quality — light, space, and calm.","zh":"他的攝影有一種治癒的特質——光線、空間和平靜。"},{"en":"Soothing content is not boring — it is deeply needed.","zh":"治癒系內容不是無聊的——它是深深被需要的。"},{"en":"She has healing energy in person too — people feel safe around her.","zh":"她本人也有治癒的能量——人們在她身邊感到安全。"}]},{"zh":"潑天富貴","pinyin":"pō tiān fù guì","en":"unexpected windfall / overwhelming blessing","description":"突然降臨的巨大機遇或財富，完全出乎意料","sentences":[{"en":"She went viral overnight and the opportunities just poured in — unexpected windfall.","zh":"她一夜之間爆紅，機會就像傾瀉而來——潑天富貴。"},{"en":"He was not prepared for the overwhelming blessing that came his way.","zh":"他沒有準備好迎接那個潑天的富貴。"},{"en":"Unexpected windfalls are exciting — but can also be overwhelming.","zh":"意想不到的潑天富貴令人興奮——但也可能讓人不知所措。"},{"en":"An overwhelming blessing is only beneficial if you are ready to receive it.","zh":"潑天富貴只有在你準備好接受時才是有益的。"},{"en":"She got the windfall she always dreamed of — and it was terrifying.","zh":"她得到了她一直夢想的潑天富貴——它是可怕的。"},{"en":"Being ready for the unexpected blessing is just as important as wanting it.","zh":"為潑天富貴做好準備和渴望它一樣重要。"},{"en":"The company offered him an unexpected windfall — a huge contract out of nowhere.","zh":"公司給了他一個意想不到的大機遇——一個突如其來的巨大合同。"},{"en":"An overwhelming blessing requires wisdom to manage well.","zh":"潑天富貴需要智慧才能好好把握。"},{"en":"She shared her unexpected windfall with the people who helped her get there.","zh":"她把她的潑天富貴分享給了幫助她到達那裡的人。"},{"en":"Not everyone can handle an overwhelming blessing — be careful what you wish for.","zh":"不是每個人都能承受潑天富貴——小心你的願望。"}]},{"zh":"搞錢","pinyin":"gǎo qián","en":"hustle / make money / grind","description":"努力賺錢，想盡辦法增加收入","sentences":[{"en":"She has three side hustles — fully in hustle mode.","zh":"她有三份副業——完全進入了搞錢模式。"},{"en":"He is always looking for new ways to make money — classic hustler.","zh":"他總是在找新的賺錢方式——典型的搞錢人。"},{"en":"Hustle culture is appealing until it burns you out.","zh":"搞錢文化很吸引人，直到它讓你倦怠。"},{"en":"She monetised her hobby and now makes money doing what she loves.","zh":"她把她的愛好變現了，現在靠做她喜歡的事賺錢。"},{"en":"In this economy, everyone is in make-money mode.","zh":"在這個經濟環境下，每個人都在搞錢。"},{"en":"He grinds all week and spends the weekend doing nothing — fair trade.","zh":"他整週搞錢，週末什麼都不做——這是公平的交易。"},{"en":"Making money is not everything but financial security matters.","zh":"搞錢不是一切，但財務安全很重要。"},{"en":"She built her hustle into a full business over three years.","zh":"她在三年內把她的搞錢副業建成了一個完整的生意。"},{"en":"Hustle hard, rest harder — that is the balance.","zh":"努力搞錢，更努力休息——這就是平衡。"},{"en":"He knows making money is a means, not an end.","zh":"他知道搞錢是手段，而不是目的。"}]},{"zh":"上岸","pinyin":"shàng àn","en":"made it / passed the big exam / achieved the goal","description":"經過長期努力，終於通過考試、找到好工作或達到目標","sentences":[{"en":"She finally passed the civil service exam — she made it after three attempts.","zh":"她終於通過了公務員考試——三次嘗試後她上岸了。"},{"en":"He got the graduate school offer — two years of studying finally paid off.","zh":"他收到了研究生院的錄取通知——兩年的學習終於有了回報，上岸了。"},{"en":"Making it to the other side after years of effort — that is the best feeling.","zh":"多年努力後終於上岸——那是最好的感覺。"},{"en":"She celebrated making it with the people who supported her.","zh":"她和支持她的人一起慶祝上岸。"},{"en":"The goal was to make it before thirty — she did it at twenty-nine.","zh":"目標是在三十歲前上岸——她在二十九歲做到了。"},{"en":"Achieving the goal feels surreal after wanting it for so long.","zh":"在渴望了這麼久之後，上岸感覺不真實。"},{"en":"He made it on his own terms — no shortcuts, no compromises.","zh":"他以自己的方式上岸——沒有捷徑，沒有妥協。"},{"en":"Making it means something different to everyone.","zh":"上岸對每個人來說意義不同。"},{"en":"She made it — and immediately started helping others do the same.","zh":"她上岸了——立刻開始幫助其他人做同樣的事情。"},{"en":"The road to making it was long but she never questioned the destination.","zh":"上岸的路很長，但她從未懷疑過目的地。"}]},{"zh":"好嗑","pinyin":"hǎo kē","en":"I ship this / so good together / love this pairing","description":"對某對CP或組合感到非常喜歡，迫切想看他們在一起","sentences":[{"en":"I ship this couple so hard — every interaction is chemistry.","zh":"我太喜歡這對CP了——每次互動都有化學反應。"},{"en":"She and her co-star have energy that makes everyone ship them.","zh":"她和她的搭檔有讓所有人都嗑CP的能量。"},{"en":"That duo is so good together — friendship goals, honestly.","zh":"那對組合太合拍了——真的是友誼目標。"},{"en":"I ship this fictional couple more than any real couple I know.","zh":"我比我認識的任何真實情侶都更嗑這對虛構CP。"},{"en":"The chemistry in that scene was undeniable — everyone noticed.","zh":"那一幕的化學反應是無可否認的——所有人都注意到了。"},{"en":"She ships this pairing so hard she made a whole playlist for them.","zh":"她太嗑這對CP了，專門為他們做了一個播放清單。"},{"en":"I love this content duo — their energy together is just right.","zh":"我很喜歡這個內容組合——他們在一起的能量剛剛好。"},{"en":"Shipping fictional characters is a whole hobby and I am here for it.","zh":"嗑虛構人物的CP是一種完整的愛好，我完全支持。"},{"en":"They said they are just friends but we all ship them.","zh":"他們說只是朋友，但我們都嗑他們了。"},{"en":"The author ships them too — it is obvious in every scene they wrote.","zh":"作者也嗑他們——在他們寫的每一幕裡都很明顯。"}]},{"zh":"凡爾賽","pinyin":"fán ěr sài","en":"humblebragging / stealth flexing","description":"用看似謙遜或抱怨的方式，其實是在炫耀自己的優越生活","sentences":[{"en":"She humblebragged about her Paris problems — 'hard to choose between two penthouses.'","zh":"她抱怨巴黎的煩惱——「很難在兩間頂層公寓之間選擇」——完全在凡爾賽。"},{"en":"That post is pure humblebragging — 'I am so tired from all these invitations.'","zh":"那篇帖子純粹是凡爾賽——「我被這麼多邀請弄得好累」。"},{"en":"He stealth-flexed his promotion by complaining how busy it would make him.","zh":"他通過抱怨升職後會有多忙來悄悄炫耀，完全是凡爾賽。"},{"en":"Humblebragging is so common on social media it has become a genre.","zh":"凡爾賽在社交媒體上如此普遍，以至於它已成為一種類型。"},{"en":"She did not realise she was humblebragging — she genuinely meant it as a complaint.","zh":"她沒有意識到她在凡爾賽——她真的把它當成投訴。"},{"en":"'I just hate how fast I lose weight when I travel' — classic humblebragging.","zh":"「我就是討厭旅行的時候瘦得那麼快」——經典凡爾賽。"},{"en":"Stealth flexing is just showing off with extra steps.","zh":"凡爾賽只是多繞了幾步的炫耀。"},{"en":"He perfected the art of the humblebrag without anyone calling him out.","zh":"他完善了凡爾賽的藝術，沒有人指出來。"},{"en":"Genuine humility is the opposite of humblebragging.","zh":"真正的謙遜是凡爾賽的反面。"},{"en":"She laughed at herself when someone pointed out her humblebragging.","zh":"當有人指出她在凡爾賽時，她笑了。"}]},{"zh":"尷尬癌","pinyin":"gān gà ái","en":"secondhand embarrassment / cringe","description":"看到別人尷尬的行為，自己也跟著感到難堪","sentences":[{"en":"I got so much secondhand embarrassment watching that speech.","zh":"看那個演講我感到嚴重的尷尬癌。"},{"en":"That cringe scene is unwatchable — I have to cover my eyes.","zh":"那個尷尬的場景太難看了——我不得不捂住眼睛。"},{"en":"His audition was so awkward I felt the secondhand embarrassment from here.","zh":"他的試鏡太尷尬了，我在這裡都感受到了尷尬癌。"},{"en":"She cringe-watched the whole thing with her hands over her face.","zh":"她用手捂著臉，裹著尷尬癌看完了整個東西。"},{"en":"Secondhand embarrassment is real — your mirror neurons work overtime.","zh":"尷尬癌是真實的——你的鏡像神經元在加班。"},{"en":"That show relies entirely on cringe humour — I cannot watch it.","zh":"那個節目完全依賴尷尬喜劇——我看不下去。"},{"en":"He posted the video without watching it back — full cringe later.","zh":"他沒有回看就發布了視頻——後來感受到了完整的尷尬。"},{"en":"She has zero secondhand embarrassment — she laughs with them.","zh":"她完全沒有尷尬癌——她和他們一起笑。"},{"en":"Cringe culture is often just judging people for being vulnerable.","zh":"尷尬癌文化往往只是因為別人展現脆弱而評判他們。"},{"en":"He used to cringe at his old videos — now he finds them charming.","zh":"他以前看到自己的舊視頻會有尷尬癌——現在他覺得它們很可愛。"}]},{"zh":"發刀","pinyin":"fā dāo","en":"heartbreaking content / emotionally devastating","description":"讓人心碎、情感上受創的內容，特指令人心痛的故事或結局","sentences":[{"en":"That ending was heartbreaking — the author sent out the knives.","zh":"那個結局太令人心碎了——作者在發刀。"},{"en":"She posted an emotionally devastating thread and the internet cried.","zh":"她發了一個令人心碎的帖子，整個網路都哭了。"},{"en":"Warning: this fic destroys you. Major heartbreaking content.","zh":"警告：這篇同人文會摧毀你，大量發刀內容。"},{"en":"He always writes heartbreaking stories — his readers love to cry.","zh":"他總是寫令人心碎的故事——他的讀者喜歡哭。"},{"en":"That documentary was emotionally devastating — I needed a week to recover.","zh":"那部紀錄片情感上非常打擊人——我需要一週才能恢復。"},{"en":"She delivered heartbreaking content in just eight seconds of a video.","zh":"她在視頻的八秒鐘內傳遞了令人心碎的內容。"},{"en":"Heartbreaking content resonates because it reflects real human experience.","zh":"發刀的內容引起共鳴，因為它反映了真實的人類體驗。"},{"en":"He served major emotional devastation and we all came back for more.","zh":"他帶來了重大的情感打擊，我們都回來求更多。"},{"en":"That plot twist was heartbreaking — I gasped out loud.","zh":"那個劇情轉折令人心碎——我大聲倒吸一口氣。"},{"en":"She warned her followers it was heartbreaking content — they read it anyway.","zh":"她警告她的粉絲這是發刀內容——他們還是看了。"}]},{"zh":"窮遊","pinyin":"qióng yóu","en":"budget travel / shoestring travel","description":"用最少的費用旅行，尋找低成本的旅遊方式","sentences":[{"en":"She budget-travelled through Southeast Asia for six months on almost nothing.","zh":"她幾乎花費極少，在東南亞預算旅行了六個月。"},{"en":"Shoestring travel taught him that experiences matter more than comfort.","zh":"窮遊教會了他體驗比舒適更重要。"},{"en":"I budget-travelled Europe with a hostel card and a backpack.","zh":"我帶著青年旅館卡和背包在歐洲窮遊。"},{"en":"The best travel memories come from shoestring adventures, not luxury hotels.","zh":"最好的旅行記憶來自窮遊，而不是豪華酒店。"},{"en":"She found the most authentic experiences while budget travelling.","zh":"她在窮遊時找到了最真實的體驗。"},{"en":"Shoestring travel requires creativity — but that is part of the fun.","zh":"窮遊需要創造力——但這就是樂趣的一部分。"},{"en":"He travelled to twenty countries on a budget — every destination worthwhile.","zh":"他在預算內去了二十個國家——每個目的地都值得。"},{"en":"Budget travel is not just cheap — it is a different way to see the world.","zh":"窮遊不只是便宜——它是看世界的另一種方式。"},{"en":"She laughs now about the struggles of her shoestring travel days.","zh":"她現在對窮遊時期的艱辛笑了起來。"},{"en":"The most interesting travellers I have met were always budget travellers.","zh":"我遇到的最有趣的旅行者總是窮遊者。"}]},{"zh":"塌房","pinyin":"tā fáng","en":"idol scandal / fell from grace / cancelled","description":"偶像或公眾人物因負面事件曝光而形象崩塌，失去粉絲支持","sentences":[{"en":"The idol had a major scandal and their career collapsed overnight.","zh":"那個偶像發生了重大醜聞，事業一夜之間崩塌了。"},{"en":"She fell from grace after leaked messages showed a different side of her.","zh":"她因洩露的訊息揭示了她不同的一面而形象崩塌。"},{"en":"The fall from grace was fast and brutal — no second chances given.","zh":"形象崩塌來得又快又殘酷——沒有給第二次機會。"},{"en":"His idol status crumbled and even loyal fans turned away.","zh":"他的偶像地位崩塌了，連忠實粉絲都轉身離去。"},{"en":"Being cancelled is the modern version of falling from grace.","zh":"被取消是現代版的形象崩塌。"},{"en":"She survived the scandal and rebuilt — more relatable than before.","zh":"她度過了醜聞，重建了形象——比以前更貼近人心。"},{"en":"The idol fell from grace but refused to disappear quietly.","zh":"那個偶像形象崩塌了，但拒絕悄悄消失。"},{"en":"Scandals can end careers or humanise public figures — depends on the response.","zh":"醜聞可以終結事業，也可以讓公眾人物更人性化——取決於回應方式。"},{"en":"He handled his fall from grace with honesty and it saved him.","zh":"他以誠實處理了形象崩塌，這救了他。"},{"en":"The internet never truly forgets a fall from grace.","zh":"網路從不真正忘記形象崩塌。"}]},{"zh":"班味","pinyin":"bān wèi","en":"corporate smell / work vibe / looking corporate","description":"身上散發出疲憊上班族的氣息，一看就是被工作壓榨的樣子","sentences":[{"en":"She came straight from the office — full corporate smell on her.","zh":"她直接從辦公室過來——身上充滿了班味。"},{"en":"His eyes had that glazed-over look — total work vibe.","zh":"他的眼睛有那種茫然的神情——完全的班味。"},{"en":"I washed the corporate energy off in a long shower after work.","zh":"我下班後洗了個長澡，把班味洗掉了。"},{"en":"That bag screams corporate — looks practical, not personal.","zh":"那個包包完全是班味——看起來實用，不個人化。"},{"en":"She detoxes from the work vibe every Friday night with friends.","zh":"她每個週五晚上和朋友一起排除班味。"},{"en":"He stepped into the bar and you could immediately see the corporate smell.","zh":"他走進酒吧，你立刻能看到他身上的班味。"},{"en":"The work vibe fades on holidays — it takes about three days.","zh":"假期能消除班味——大約需要三天。"},{"en":"I do not want to carry the corporate energy home to my family.","zh":"我不想把班味帶回家給我的家人。"},{"en":"She learned to leave the work vibe at the office — home is a sanctuary.","zh":"她學會了把班味留在辦公室——家是一個聖地。"},{"en":"His weekend self and his corporate-smell self are completely different people.","zh":"他週末的樣子和帶著班味的他完全是兩個不同的人。"}]},{"zh":"我不配","pinyin":"wǒ bù pèi","en":"I don't deserve this / imposter syndrome","description":"面對好事或機會時，感覺自己不夠好、不值得擁有","sentences":[{"en":"She got the award and immediately thought 'I do not deserve this.'","zh":"她得了獎，立刻想「我不配」。"},{"en":"Imposter syndrome made him doubt every achievement.","zh":"感覺自己不配讓他懷疑每一個成就。"},{"en":"'I do not deserve this' is what people say when they actually do.","zh":"「我不配」是真正值得的人說的話。"},{"en":"She had to consciously remind herself she earned every opportunity.","zh":"她不得不有意識地提醒自己，她贏得了每一個機會。"},{"en":"Feeling like you do not deserve good things is imposter syndrome in action.","zh":"感覺自己不配好事，就是「我不配」感在作怪。"},{"en":"He downplayed his talent so long he started believing he had none.","zh":"他貶低自己的才能太久了，以至於開始相信自己沒有。"},{"en":"You deserve good things. Say it until you believe it.","zh":"你值得好的事情，說到你相信為止。"},{"en":"The 'I do not deserve this' feeling is a sign you care about integrity.","zh":"「我不配」的感覺是你在意誠信的標誌。"},{"en":"She accepted the praise with grace instead of deflecting it.","zh":"她優雅地接受了稱讚，而不是迴避它。"},{"en":"Imposter syndrome affects even the most accomplished people.","zh":"感覺自己不配甚至影響最有成就的人。"}]}];
